"""Approximate the corporate-news and institutional-ownership response.

Training responses cluster around company labels, selected brand/news/place
names, and Chinese financial/reporting vocabulary. These word-family means
model that regularity, rather than an arbitrary activation for each token.
Products and sports are weak negative contrasts.

A company/finance cue fades by 10% per token, boosting business vocabulary
and 'its'. Possessive 's distinguishes contractions and human collectives
from company/country owners using the preceding word. Chinese company and
stock morphemes also match beyond the listed examples. State resets between
documents. Formatting markers get small fixed responses; otherwise predict
zero. Many weaker word-specific responses are intentionally left unexplained.
"""
READS = ()

# Fitted averages for recognizable word families. Case and word boundaries
# distinguish company labels from fragments of identifiers.
FAMILIES = {
