"""Negative response to short 'od' spelling fragments, in several scripts.

The largest response is to bare od and three-letter syllables ending in od.
Extra letters, plural endings, capitalization, and the onset consonant change
its strength; mod is much weaker than god or pod.  Cyrillic од and Arabic ود
behave similarly.  Related d-fragments and a few deity words respond weakly.
Most other tokens are left at zero: this is a spelling-family approximation, not a token table.
